<title>USA: EIA report 1.7 m barrle U.S. drop in propane.</title>
<headline>EIA report 1.7 m barrle U.S. drop in propane.</headline>
<text>
<p>Total U.S. stocks, at 48.7 million as of Oct. 11, are about 16 percent below levels this time last year.</p>
<p>The industry prefers a comfort level of 60 million barrels going into winter, a goal market players doubt will be reached.</p>
<p>&quot;This is a very bullish report,&quot; said one Houston player.</p>
<p>Upon release of the report, propane was heard trading at 50.65 cents, about a half cent higher than in earlier activity.</p>
<p>-- Laney Salisbury New York Energy Desk 1212-859-1631</p>
</text>
